The workspace-wide resolver is currently contaminated by another in-progress worker’s uncached ACP dependency, so I’ve isolated only 2.9 and its real transitive crates under `/tmp` for compiler/test feedback. That preserves the shared checkout and still exercises the actual task code and actual `keith-skills` filesystem registry—not mocks.
